In my Laravel application, I've implemented a function callAi() which uses the orhanerday/open-ai package to interact with the GPT API for generating responses in a chat interface. Below is the code snippet for this function:
use Orhanerday\OpenAi\OpenAi;

public function __construct()
{
    $this->open_ai_key = env('OPEN_IA_KEY');
    $this->open_ai = new OpenAi($this->open_ai_key);
}

public function callAi($prompt)
{
    try {
        $complete = $this->open_ai->chat([
            "model" => 'gpt-3.5-turbo-0125',
            'messages' => $prompt,
            'temperature' => 0.3,
            'max_tokens' => 50,
            'frequency_penalty' => 0,
            'presence_penalty' => 0.6
        ]);
    } catch (Exception $e) {
        Log::error(["Call AI error:" => $e]);
        return $e->getMessage();
    }

    return $complete;
}

The prompt parameter passed to callAi() is an array containing role-based messages, each with specific content. Here's an example format of the prompt array:
[
    [
        "role" => "system",
